From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: C906 L1 caches have 256 sets each

The C906 L1 data cache is 64 KiB, 4-way, and the instruction cache 32 KiB,
2-way, both with 64-byte lines: 256 sets each. The device tree had 512
data and 128 instruction sets, from which the kernel's cacheinfo derives
the associativities the other way round (data 2-way, instructions 4-way)
and reports them in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cache.

Measured on an SG2002 (NanoKVM):

- Data, by pointer chasing in physically contiguous memory with
  interrupts off: a hit costs 3 ns, a miss 161 ns (no L2). Random sets of
  up to 32 KiB hit, 128 KiB miss (64 KiB). Sequential loads cost twice as
  much per doubling of the stride up to 64 bytes (line). Lines 16, 32 or
  64 KiB apart all hit for up to 4 lines and miss from 5 or 6; 8 KiB
  apart up to 8 (4 ways of 16 KiB).
- Instructions, by chasing jumps through code generated in user space
  (virtual addresses, arbitrary physical pages; the exact thresholds
  at virtual strides mean the index is virtual): up to 32 KiB of
  lines hit (3 ns per block), 64 KiB miss (120-165 ns). Blocks 16, 32 or
  64 KiB apart hit for up to 2 and miss from 3; 8 KiB apart up to 4,
  4 KiB apart up to 8 (2 ways of 16 KiB).
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x-cpus.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x-cpus.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x-cpus.dtsi
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x-cpus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/cv180x-cpus.dtsi
@@ -15,10 +15,10 @@
 			device_type = "cpu";
 			reg = <0>;
 			d-cache-block-size = <64>;
-			d-cache-sets = <512>;
+			d-cache-sets = <256>;
 			d-cache-size = <65536>;
 			i-cache-block-size = <64>;
-			i-cache-sets = <128>;
+			i-cache-sets = <256>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			mmu-type = "riscv,sv39";
 			riscv,isa = "rv64imafdc";
